    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "2bb72eb7_677a7218",
        "filename": "chip/npcx/system.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 855,
      "author": {
        "id": 1121210
      },
      "writtenOn": "2016-09-09T03:46:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Indeed, it\u0027s a little tricky. At the beginning I developed the utilities located in suspend ram, the original ec.lds.S looked like:\n\n1. Add a 1568 bytes memory declaration, LPRAM, in MEMORY section.\n2. Add a lowpower_ram section and declare it is loaded from flash to lpram. (ie. \"} \u003e LPRAM AT \u003e FLASH\")\n\nBut during the arranging the memory mapping of ec with Shawn, I don\u0027t want to add the complexity of linker script and put them in .text section together. It should be OK since we keep it small and doesn\u0027t touch any data in rodata section. Any local const data related to function is put in text region. (For example, register addresses.) It will be copied to suspend ram, too.\n\nThere\u0027s is another method to achieve this. Put __start_gdma() in the end of CDRAM. Kick off GDMA to move the other region from flash to ram. (Exclude itself.) Make sure the length and address meet 16 bytes aligned. But since it didn\u0027t move itself from RW region. I think there\u0027s side effect during computing hash value of RW region. That\u0027s why I move it into lpram. It\u0027s simpler.",
      "parentUuid": "f68dffb6_0c69ffee",
      "revId": "d5915f40ad2ac8252c0b27def083f4f01d479ac2",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "4b1e22a7_eb4d2d90",
        "filename": "chip/npcx/system.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 855,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002124
      },
      "writtenOn": "2016-09-09T17:41:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "that\u0027s great you sorted through these things, but you really need to add comments in these files indicating what\u0027s actually happening. It\u0027s not clear from someone who is picking this up and looking at what is currently going on. \n\nMoreover, these functions should be marked __attribute__((noreturn)) so that 1. it provide more information to the reader and 2. let\u0027s the compiler perform certain optimizations.",
      "parentUuid": "2bb72eb7_677a7218",
      "revId": "d5915f40ad2ac8252c0b27def083f4f01d479ac2",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
